cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If QUARTIC2D contributes to published research, cite the archived software release used in the calculation."
title: "QUARTIC2D: Angular-Harmonic Evaluation of Four-Center Interactions in Two Dimensions"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  QUARTIC2D evaluates four-center interaction matrix elements for localized
  two-dimensional states with translationally invariant radial kernels. The
  method represents general real or complex transition fields in angular
  harmonics and reduces the interaction to radial Hankel integrals. The same
  formulation applies to direct, exchange, pair-hopping, correlated-hopping,
  and other four-index orbital channels within the radial-kernel assumption.
authors:
  - family-names: "Santacruz"
    given-names: "Alex"
keywords:
  - four-center interactions
  - interaction matrix elements
  - Hankel transform
  - angular harmonics
  - two-dimensional materials
  - quantum materials
  - Wannier functions
repository-code: "https://github.com/QuantumArtificer/quartic2d"
url: "https://quantumartificer.github.io/quartic2d/"
license: MIT
